  "summary": "Today's health-tech landscape highlights several major momentum shifts. Major insurers UnitedHealth, Cigna, and Centene have adopted a shared credentialing platform through CertifyOS, streamlining provider onboarding across multiple plans. Meanwhile, significant funding rounds underscore investor confidence in specialized health tech: Rightway raised $155 million for pharmacy benefits technology and Precision Neuroscience secured $250 million for brain-computer interfaces. On the regulatory front, Heidi Overton's FDA commissioner nomination hearing emphasized speed and innovation to compete globally, while separately, Chris Klomp advanced toward confirmation as deputy HHS secretary. The healthcare AI transformation is accelerating across radiology and oncology, with Massachusetts General Brigham partnering with GE Healthcare on radiation oncology AI and radiology startups increasingly becoming \"AI-native\" practices. Finally, a measles outbreak reaching its worst U.S. levels since 1991—including deaths in Pennsylvania among unvaccinated populations—signals a critical public health concern as vaccination rates decline.",
